@host = http://localhost:8080

### Check that the API is up
GET {{host}}/health

### Register (the password needs an uppercase letter, a lowercase letter, a digit and a symbol)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "password": "Test1234!"
}

### Login (stores the token for the requests below)
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "password": "Test1234!"
}

### Without a token: should return 401
GET {{host}}/api/products

### Create a product
POST {{host}}/api/products
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test product",
  "description": "First test",
  "price": 9.99
}

### List products (paginated)
GET {{host}}/api/products?page=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Get a product by id
GET {{host}}/api/products/1
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Update a product
PUT {{host}}/api/products/1
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Updated product",
  "description": "New description",
  "price": 19.99
}

### Validation: empty name and negative price (should return 400)
POST {{host}}/api/products
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "price": -5
}

### Delete a product
DELETE {{host}}/api/products/1
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}